dilizia\", \"stato\": \"approvato\", \"importo\": 3595, \"responsabile\": \"Irene\", \"data\": null}, {\"id\": \"P02-021\", \"reparto\": \"impianti\", \"stato\": \"sospeso\", \"importo\": null, \"responsabile\": \"Luca\", \"data\": \"2026-11-24\"}]\nMeasurement series: [79, 6, 6, 25, 49, 29, 55, 63, 36, 81, 3, 12, 54, 84, 18, 78, 27, 0, 89, 69, 35, 65]\n\nKeep the answer concise: at most about 120 words, or the requested code or data. Do not include internal reasoning.","title_original":"Outlier · scenario 03","prompt_translation":{"method":"English task templates and deterministic context translation","sha256":"25b2166d18f71df0d9554ebf376e33036db4d764f4443316ffc3eed54ca33036","used_for_inference":false},"answer_en":"```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Dati forniti\ndata = [79, 6, 6, 25, 49, 29, 55, 63, 36, 81, 3, 12, 54, 84, 18, 78, 27, 0, 89, 69, 35, 65]\narr = np.array(data)\n\n# Calcolo statistiche robuste\nmedian = np.median(arr)\nq1 = np.percentile(arr, 25)\nq3 = np.percentile(arr, 75)\niqr = q3 - q1\n\n# Soglie (regola 1.5 * IQR)\nlower_bound = q1 - 1.5 * iqr\nupper_bound = q3 + 1.5 * iqr\n\n# Identificazione outlier\noutliers = arr[(arr < lower_bound) | (arr > upper_bound)]\n\nprint(f\"Mediana: {median}\")\nprint(f\"Q1: {q1}, Q3: {q3}, IQR: {iqr}\")\nprint(f\"Soglia inferiore: {lower_bound}\")\nprint(f\"Soglia superiore: {upper_bound}\")\nprint(f\"Outlier individuati: {outliers.tolist()}\")\n```<|im_end|>","answer_translation":{"method":"literal structured/code response","service":"Google Translate","translated_date":"2026-10-16","source_sha256":"3b6bb145a937cad12ac7fd9a73959d25df0f953275c3146cb4651e5967b0b72c","sha256":"3b6bb145a937cad12ac7fd9a73959d25df0f953275c3146cb4651e5967b0b72c","used_for_inference":false,"editorial_changes":[]},"answer_literal_glossary":[{"original":"Calcolo statistiche robuste","english":"Compute robust statistics"},{"original":"Soglie (regola 1.5 * IQR)","english":"Thresholds (1.5 * IQR rule)"},{"original":"Identificazione outlier",